    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A small <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/appanage">appanage</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moskva-river">Moskva River</a> that rose under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-nevsky">Alexander Nevsky</a>'s descendants to unite north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>.</li><li>Its princes grew rich and powerful as tribute collectors for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-horde">Golden Horde</a>, then ended <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tatars">Tatar</a> overlordship in 1480.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-iii">Ivan III</a> annexed Novgorod and Tver and rebuilt the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow-kremlin">Kremlin</a>; in 1547 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-iv-of-russia">Ivan IV</a> was crowned tsar and Muscovy became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-i-of-moscow">Ivan I</a>'s nickname Kalita means 'money bag' or 'purse', probably a reference to the wealth he amassed or to his reputed alms-giving.</p></aside>
    </section>

